  "warnings": [],
  "working_thesis": "Action and speech, rooted in human plurality and natality, constitute the human realm and generate power, but their inherent boundlessness, unpredictability, and irreversibility lead to vulnerabilities that historical traditions have attempted to remedy through making, rule, or fabrication—while the true internal remedies of action are found in the capacities of forgiving and promising."
